    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e7590966",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image depicts soldiers marching in a desert environment, with overlaid text reading 'we're getting ready to go march for free college' and 'care to join?'. The visual of military personnel is juxtaposed with the concept of 'marching for free college', implying that enlisting in the military is a required or recommended path to obtain free education. This is a form of propaganda, as it attempts to influence public opinion or behavior by associating the pursuit of free college with military service, potentially encouraging enlistment under the guise of educational opportunity. The meme does not contain overtly abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or other forms of toxicity as defined in the provided knowledge base. The intent is to promote a specific action (joining the military) by leveraging the appeal of free college, using the imagery of military readiness to frame the message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1d7d1393"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
